text:
anya: Quick pass please — pushing dark-mode token heatmap for Console charts. Figma: https://www.figma.com/file/abcd1234. Main concerns: low-value tokens are nearly invisible in legend, code block syntax looks washed, tooltip bg feels too transparent. Screenshot attached.
sam: Agree on low tokens. They disappear at gamma=1. Can we raise midtones or add a perceptual ramp? Also small legend dots lose contrast.
michael: Frontend note — we use a linear colormap now; for counts a log or power scale helps. Small cells fail contrast, especially at 1-2px widths.
joy: Accessibility reminder: aim for WCAG AA for static text (4.5:1 for small text). For heatmaps consider adding non-color cues (patterns/borders) for low buckets — helps colorblind users. ColorBrewer ‘PuOr’ or a viridis-like perceptual map could work.
anya: cc @joy good call. Also copy tweak: current legend uses labels like "low" / "med" — ambiguous. Suggest explicit ranges.
sam: Proposed labels: "Rare (<=5%)", "Occasional (6–20%)", "Common (21–60%)", "Frequent (>60%)". For syntax blocks, current fg #cbd5e1 on bg #0b0f12 reads flat; maybe nudge fg to #e6eef8 or warm the bg to #0e1114.
michael: Quick CSS prototype for outline/hover:
```
:root {
  --bg-code: #0e1114;
  --code-fg: #e6eef8;
  --token-low: #0f1720;
  --token-mid: #234b6a;
  --token-high: #7cc6ff;
}
.heatmap .cell.low { outline: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.04); }
.heatmap .cell:hover { box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(2,6,23,0.6); transform: translateY(-1px); }
```
design-bot: Auto-contrast-check results: legend text #98a2b3 on bg #0b0f12 -> contrast 4.1:1 (small text fails AA). Recommend #b8c3d1 or bold weight.
joy: Also: avoid only color differences for adjacent bins. Try 1px inner stroke for low bins and a subtle pattern (dots) layer for <5% bucket in PNG exports. Tooltips: bump opacity to 0.92 and use 2px shadow for separation. Keyboard focus must have a visible ring (3px solid #3b82f6) and aria-labels on canvas cells.
anya: OK. Can someone mock two variations in Figma: A) saturated accent + thin outline, B) desaturated ramp + pattern overlay for lowest bucket. I'll run a quick A/B with the metrics team. Targeting this for next sprint.
sam: I'll update Figma and the legend copy. Quick poll in thread: outline (:+1:) or pattern (:-1:)?
michael: I'll prototype the outline approach in the demo branch and add the accessibility hooks. /assign @michael
joy: One more nit — exported heatmap PNGs need alt text and a short caption describing the color mapping (e.g., "Color scale shows token frequency: Rare <=5% ..."). Otherwise screen readers get nothing.
anya: Great — thanks everyone. Will upload figma variants by EOD and link here.
